Z||000000||jubjub2m6||11-13-2001||07:06 PM||||I just recently installed polyurethane bushings in my front control arms.(Old wones were pretty toast) I put the new ones in greased them up did everything they said to but the things squeak like there is no tommorow. My friend has poly on his car also and it squeaks like 1/4 as much whats going on? I also replaced the back bushings with poly those dont squeak hardly at all...This baffles me. Can anyone help me with having to tear the suspension apart all over again? I can live with the squeak cause it does make a difference handling wise but just wander if anyone has any tips.<BR><P>------------------<BR>86SE Gold Modified<BR>To many mods to list<BR>http://www.geocities.com/kingjubjub/fiero/||||reg||5
Z||000001||shark93726||11-13-2001||08:00 PM||||Firstly, where did you put the grease?<P>It needs to be between the steel sleeve and the poly, and it needs to be on the ends of the poly. The ends probably squeak more than the center hole will. (just guessing on this)<P>Some poly bushings, which are molded, seem to be a tighter fit, which may make the squeaking worse.<P>Hope you get it cured.<P>I am selling U.H.M.W. polyethylene bushings, (with offsets for extra adjustment) which do not squeak.  If you are interested, you can read about them on my web site<P>Gerald Storvik (8shark.com)||||reg||1
